{
 "_comment": [
  "THE CI SHARD PARTITION OF THE PHPUNIT SUITE.",
  "",
  "bin/verify-shard-partition.php PROVES this file is a total, disjoint partition of",
  "the suite: every test the committed phpunit.xml.dist collects is run by exactly one",
  "shard, by comparing the sets PHPUnit itself collects. It is not a comment, and it is",
  "not a count of directories — a plausible misspelling of a path is exactly how a test",
  "goes missing, and a directory count stays happy when it happens.",
  "",
  "BOUNDARIES ARE MEASURED, NOT GUESSED. Each shard was cut from the per-file wall times",
  "this repository actually produced; see ci/shard-timings.md for the per-area table, the",
  "command that produced it, the measurements that had to be VOIDED and re-taken, and the",
  "red areas that are other lanes' business. A shard boundary chosen from a guess is a",
  "boundary that will be wrong on the next schema change.",
  "",
  "A shard may name a tests/ area, a subdirectory, or a single file. Where an area is much",
  "heavier than the mean it is subdivided, because a directory is the coarsest unit that",
  "fits and tests/Ingest (2201s measured alone) needs finer than that."
 ],
